# Your own private identifiers, one grep pattern per line.
#
# scripts/preflight_public.sh greps the whole tree for these and refuses to let
# you publish if any of them appears. Copy this file to .private-identifiers,
# which is gitignored, and put your real values in it.
#
# The point of keeping them out of the tracked script: an earlier version of the
# preflight hard-coded them, which published the very list it existed to enforce.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Everything else is treated
# as an extended regular expression, so escape dots in domains.

# Your name, and any spelling of it that appears in your documents
Your Full Name
Yourname

# Your account handles
your-github-handle

# Your institutions, employers and their domains
Your University
youruniversity\.edu

# People you work with, whose names must never appear in a public repo
Your Supervisor

# Your project and product names
YOURPROJECT
